<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n88524" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσανα-βαίνω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-βήσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Eq.Mag.</u>
					1.2
				</span></i>
			:—<i>go up,</i> or <i>mount besides,</i> l. c.;
			of water-birds, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. πρὸς τὰς πέτρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					617a26
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. πρὸς τὸ ὄρθιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					39.45
				</span></i>
			; <i>rise higher,</i> as a swollen river, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.72.4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλις προσαναβαίνουσα</span>”
				<i>lying on a mountain side,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					9.20
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τῷ Ῥωμύλῳ</span>
			<i>go back as far as</i> R., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Thes.</u>
				1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. acc.
			loci, <i>climb, ascend,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ σιμόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.Com.
					79
				</span></i>
			.</div>
